SSOR for any finding, and TC-334 doesn't test the bound. The only checks sit under SR-233, as LLR-311's direction clause and TC-332's text assertion.\n- **It reads like a guarantee about the judge's output**, but only prompt text backs it. Since this bound is what keeps a fail-open finding from being deferred out of the lane, the record should say honestly what holds it. This is the same defect class as the SR-154 return in WI-913.\n\n**The disposition draft asks the lane to:**\n- move the bound into SR-234's requirement, as something the delivered directions do;\n- give it a verifying child, by adding SR-234 to LLR-311's SR-Refs or stating it in LLR-314, with TC-334 asserting the directions clause;\n- re-sit SR-234 together with SR-233 and SR-236.\n\nThe coordinator needs to carry the draft.\n\n**Advisory:** no spine row says that a SUCCESSOR ruling actually produces the successor row it promises. Per the spec's Trust section, filing it is a coordinator step at landing. If that should be attested rather than procedural, it needs a requirement home.\n\nThe untracked `010-ADJUDICATE-cdcd10e.md.requested` belongs to the coordinator, and I didn't touch it.","ttft_ms":32074,"type":"result","duration_ms":258842,"uuid":"5ab3ddd3-8c08-49d2-a35e-4f968178edb8","ttft_stream_ms":15361,"time_to_request_ms":291,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":22,"system_prompt":37,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":162,"input_hooks":2,"transcript_persist":1,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":9,"engine_pickup":2,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":3,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":14,"client_creation":6,"request_build":13},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":69,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":374,"time_to_request_major_faults":26475,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"changed_files","slowest_producer_ms":153,"cpu_ms":173,"major_faults":22049,"change