{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg56dmsCPThBWM774j9z2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All ten rows changed meaning. I blessed and re-anchored the eight LLR and TC rows. SR-234 goes back for one clause, which leaves the two other SRs blessed but unanchored behind it. Two commits, each ending `WI: WI-911`, and the commit checks passed on both:\n\n| Commit | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `bbbe4035e` | The verdict under `## amendment`, with a `## Dispositions` draft, `VERDICT: MEANING rows=10` and `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment`. The kit's parser accepts it under this sitting's combined binding. |\n| `dcadf1481` | `snapshot --reattests` for LLR-069, LLR-311, LLR-313, LLR-314, TC-069, TC-332, TC-333 and TC-334. Only the LLR and TC registries were copied. |\n\n| Rows | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| LLR-313, TC-333 (review stance, reading scopes, registry lines, plan-critique reachability gates) | Blessed and anchored |\n| LLR-069, TC-069 (an accepted DISMISS *or SUCCESSOR* resolves a rework exclusion; the plan cap stays DISMISS-only) | Blessed and anchored |\n| LLR-311, TC-332 (reachability-tied severity, contrived scenarios, re-grading, the promise bound, convergence directions) | Blessed and anchored |\n| LLR-314, TC-334 (SUCCESSOR as a fourth parsed ruling; TC-334 tier Smoke → Full) | Blessed and anchored |\n| SR-233, SR-236 | Blessed, but unanchored behind SR-234 |\n| **SR-234** | **Not blessed** |\n\nEach row's new arms match the code. The dispute parser's ruling order is FIX, SUCCESSOR, DISMISS, ESCALATE. The coverage gate resolves on DISMISS or SUCCESSOR while the plan cap stays DISMISS-only. The dispute template rules out SUCCESSOR for fail-open, data-loss or Done-when-gap findings. Every cited test exists, and TC-334's `Full` tier is honest because `test_dispute` only runs in the full suite.\n\n**Why SR-234 goes back:** adding \"a successor row\" to the ruling set is fine. The new acceptance clause \"the dispute sitting never selects SUCCESSOR for a fail-open, data-loss, or Done-when-gap finding\" is the problem:\n- **Not in the requirement.** The requirement allows a successor row with no restriction.\n- **Nothing under SR-234 implements or checks it.** The parser accepts SUCCESSOR for any finding, and TC-334 doesn't test the bound. The only checks sit under SR-233, as LLR-311's direction clause and TC-332's text assertion.\n- **It reads like a guarantee about the judge's output**, but only prompt text backs it. Since this bound is what keeps a fail-open finding from being deferred out of the lane, the record should say honestly what holds it. This is the same defect class as the SR-154 return in WI-913.\n\n**The disposition draft asks the lane to:**\n- move the bound into SR-234's requirement, as something the delivered directions do;\n- give it a verifying child, by adding SR-234 to LLR-311's SR-Refs or stating it in LLR-314, with TC-334 asserting the directions clause;\n- re-sit SR-234 together with SR-233 and SR-236.\n\nThe coordinator needs to carry the draft.\n\n**Advisory:** no spine row says that a SUCCESSOR ruling actually produces the successor row it promises. Per the spec's Trust section, filing it is a coordinator step at landing. If that should be attested rather than procedural, it needs a requirement home.\n\nThe untracked `010-ADJUDICATE-cdcd10e.md.requested` belongs to the coordinator, and I didn't touch it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1047,"cache_read_input_tokens":522197,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1047},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"0c278fdf-3f61-4fd1-b65d-05a91d94